# Expected: NIKA-PARSE-017 at CHECK.
nika: e05-parse-duplicate-id
# INTENT: two tasks under one `tasks:` mapping may not share an id — the file
# must be REFUSED, never resolved by silent last-wins.
# The refusal lands at the mapping layer: repeating `step:` IS a duplicate
# mapping key, so NIKA-PARSE-017 fires before the task-id rule
# (NIKA-PARSE-007) is ever consulted. Both are spec rows (05 §parse); this
# shape cannot reach PARSE-007, because two same-id tasks in one mapping are
# always the same bytes as a duplicate key. The law under test is the
# no-last-wins refusal; the code that carries it is PARSE-017.
tasks:
  step:
    exec:
      command: ["echo", "first"]
  step:
    exec:
      command: ["echo", "second"]
